---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { loadSiteContent } from '../lib/content';

const { showNotes } = await loadSiteContent();
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Don Yuen: a software engineer who likes to build things from first principles and make them accessible."
  showNotes={showNotes}
>
  <div class="page prose">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      I'm Don Yuen, a software engineer. I like to understand a system all the
      way down, then build something other people can use.
    </p>
    <p>
      I took computer science courses at CUNY. My final project for a CS class
      became the Historic Photo Explorer: a Node.js server, built only from
      Node's core modules, that searches the Library of Congress and asks the
      Claude API to describe photos for blind and visually impaired readers.
    </p>
    <p>
      To learn how machine learning works underneath the frameworks, I wrote a
      neural network in plain NumPy, derived backpropagation by hand, and
      checked it against numerical gradients before trusting a single result.
    </p>

    <h2>The engineering I like</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Working from first principles.</strong> Writing the parts myself
        until I know what each one does, then deciding what to depend on.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Measuring before claiming.</strong> Repeating runs across seeds,
        scoring outputs against a rubric, and saying plainly what a number does
        and doesn't show.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Accessibility.</strong> Building for people who use screen
        readers, keyboards and small phones, not only for the default case.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>APIs and servers.</strong> Keeping keys on the server, escaping
        everything that reaches the page, and handling timeouts and errors in
        one place.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .lede {
    margin-top: 16px;
    font-size: clamp(21px, 3.4vw, 26px);
    line-height: 1.35;
  }
</style>
